---
import BaseLayout from '@layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import SectionBand from '@components/SectionBand.astro';
import Button from '@components/Button.astro';
import AlumniGallery from '@components/AlumniGallery.astro';
import { practice } from '@data/site';
import { alumni } from '@data/alumni';

const title = 'Admin and medical assistant careers';
const description =
  'A small, physician-owned dermatology practice in Dana Point, hiring front-office staff and medical assistants — permanent roles, plus a pre-PA mentoring path. How to apply.';
---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} path="/join-us/">
  <!-- 1 · Hero -->
  <SectionBand as="div" class="hero">
    <div class="hero__copy" data-reveal>
      <span class="eyebrow">Join us</span>
      <h1>We’re a small, physician-owned practice, and we’re hiring.</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        Advanced Dermatology has been in Dana Point since 2006 — physician-owned, independent, one
        building, one team of about seventeen staff.
      </p>
      <p class="hero__hiring">
        We’re hiring for two kinds of roles: front office and medical assistant.
      </p>
      <div class="hero__cta">
        <Button href="#apply" variant="primary">Apply</Button>
        <Button href="#mentoring" variant="secondary">The mentoring path ↓</Button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 2 · The roles -->
  <SectionBand id="roles" tone="fog" aria-labelledby="roles-heading">
    <div class="prose" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="roles-heading">The roles</h2>

      <h3>Medical assistant</h3>
      <p>
        You’re in the exam rooms from week one — rooming patients, taking history, setting up and
        assisting with biopsies and excisions, working alongside Dr. Lander on Mohs days, assisting
        cosmetic procedures, handling callbacks, documenting visits. The room turns over fast and
        the day stays full.
      </p>
      <p>
        You’re given real responsibility early, so the first few months are a lot to absorb. Some
        people use the role for a year or two of clinical experience before PA or medical school.
        Others build a career here. We hire for both, and neither one is the fallback option.
      </p>
      <p>
        The role fits you if you want hands-on clinical work, you’re reliable and quick to learn,
        and you’re comfortable being told when something’s wrong. It’s a harder fit if you need a
        slow, predictable pace and a fixed schedule — the exam rooms don’t work that way.
      </p>

      <h3>Administrative</h3>
      <p>
        You run the front office — scheduling, patient coordination, billing. It’s steadier work
        than the exam rooms, by design, and it’s meant to be a long-term seat, not a stepping
        stone.
      </p>
      <p>
        In a practice this size, the front desk isn’t one of forty. You know the patients who come
        through, and you work directly with the providers, not through three layers of management.
      </p>
      <p>
        The seat fits you if you’re organized, steady, and good with patients on the phone and at
        the desk, and you want to stay somewhere a while. You don’t need a clinical background.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="roles__cta" data-reveal>
      <Button href="#apply" variant="primary">Apply</Button>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 3 · The mentoring path -->
  <SectionBand id="mentoring" tone="evergreen" aria-labelledby="path-heading">
    <div class="prose prose--on-dark" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="path-heading">The mentoring path</h2>
      <p>
        For about twenty years, this practice has also been a place pre-PA and pre-med graduates
        come to get their clinical hours. It isn’t a classroom program. You work next to
        Dr. Moinfar and the physician assistants and learn the way they did — seeing the conditions
        in person, hearing how a diagnosis gets made, doing the parts you’re cleared to do and
        watching the rest.
      </p>
      <p>
        More than 100 people have come through that way, and a number of them are physician
        assistants or physicians now. Madeline Fee and Shylie Falahati, two of the physician
        assistants on staff, both started here as medical assistants, went to PA school, and came
        back.
      </p>
      <p>
        If that’s your plan, we hire knowing it. When you’re ready to apply, you leave with
        clinical hours that hold up, a reference from the dermatologist who trained you, and help
        thinking through where to apply. Dermatology has a turnover problem; here, the people who
        leave leave for a reason we’re glad to have been part of.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 4 · Where they are now -->
  <SectionBand aria-labelledby="now-heading">
    <p class="now__intro" data-reveal>
      As alumni give us permission to include them, this is where the last twenty years have gone.
      Names and photos are added only with a signed release.
    </p>
    <AlumniGallery heading="Where they are now" entries={alumni} />
  </SectionBand>

  <!-- 5 · Apply -->
  <SectionBand id="apply" tone="evergreen-deep" aria-labelledby="cta-heading">
    <div class="closing" data-reveal>
      <h2 id="cta-heading">Apply</h2>
      <p>
        Send a resume and a short note about the role you want and why now. If it’s a fit, we’ll
        bring you in to meet the team and see the clinic.
      </p>
      <div class="closing__cta">
        <Button
          href="mailto:derm@dermsc.com?subject=Application"
          variant="primary"
        >
          Email your resume
        </Button>
        <Button href={`tel:${practice.phoneHref}`} variant="secondary">
          Call {practice.phone}
        </Button>
      </div>
      <p class="closing__cross">
        Want to know how the practice is set up first?
        <a class="link-underline" href="/about/">About Advanced Dermatology</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </SectionBand>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  /* Hero — padding-block from .section; h1 → .lede gap is global. */
  .hero__hiring {
    margin-top: var(--space-6);
    max-width: var(--wrap-prose);
  }

  /* Roles — apply CTA under the prose */
  .roles__cta {
    max-width: var(--wrap-prose);
    margin-top: var(--space-12);
  }

  /* Where they are now */
  .now__intro {
    max-width: var(--wrap-prose);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    color: var(--stone);
  }

  /* Closing — .closing / .closing__cta are shared; only the cross-link note is local */
  .closing__cross {
    margin-top: var(--space-8);
    color: var(--stone);
  }
</style>
